# ATP Site Management — Workflow Documentation

> **System:** Reengineering Budget Tracking Tool  
> **Updated:** April 2026  
> **Audience:** Field Engineers, Operations, Admin Backoffice

---

## Overview

The system manages telecom site re-engineering work orders (ATP) across a multi-stage operational lifecycle. Navigation is powered by a **Chrome-style persistent tab system** — multiple work orders can stay open simultaneously without losing context.

---

## 1. Navigation Architecture

The application supports two paths to reach the ATP work environment:

```mermaid
graph TD
    A([User Logs In]) --> B{Where to go?}

    B -->|Fast Track| C["/projects/type/filter/sites\nor /sites?tab=active"]
    B -->|Browse| D["/sites — Site Registry"]

    C -->|Click ATP Number column| E["🔗 ATP Number Link"]
    D -->|Search / filter site| F["Click Site Name or Site ID"]

    F --> G["/sites/{siteId} — Site Detail Page"]
    G -->|Click Pekerjaan tab| H["ATP Work Order Table"]
    H -->|Click 'Buka →' button| E

    E -->|openTab()| I["🗂️ New App Tab Opens"]
    I --> J["/atp/{workOrderId} — ATP Work Page"]

    style J fill:#2563eb,color:#fff,stroke:#1d4ed8
    style E fill:#059669,color:#fff,stroke:#047857
```

### Key Principle
> **Two valid entry points. One destination. One active ATP per site.**

---

## 2. ATP Work Page Layout (`/atp/{id}`)

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph Header["📌 Header — Always Visible"]
        H1["ATP Number  ·  Sektor Badge  ·  Type  ·  Status"]
        H2["Meta Row (inline-editable):\nSite ID · PO · SOW · SOW Type · Asset Element · Capex Project · Batch"]
    end

    subgraph Stepper["🪜 Stage Stepper"]
        S1["1·Imported"] --> S2["2·Permit"] --> S3["3·Implementasi"] --> S4["4·ATP"] --> S5["5·BAST"] --> S6["6·Invoice"] --> S7["7·Selesai"]
    end

    subgraph Tabs["📂 Inner Tabs"]
        T1["📋 Permit"]
        T2["🔧 Implementasi"]
        T3["📡 ATP & Dokumen"]
        T4["💰 Penagihan"]
        T5["📷 Foto (N)"]
        T6["📎 File & Lampiran"]
        T7["📜 Log"]
    end

    Header --> Stepper --> Tabs
```

---

## 3. Stage Lifecycle

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> imported : ATP Initiated
    imported --> permit : Permit Process Starts
    permit --> implementasi : Permit Released
    implementasi --> atp : RFS Done / RFI Done
    atp --> bast : ATP Checklist Complete
    bast --> invoice : BAST Signed
    invoice --> completed : Invoice Paid
    completed --> [*]

    permit --> cancelled : Permit Expired / Cancelled
    implementasi --> cancelled : Work Cancelled
```

### Stage Color Guide

| Stage | Color | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `imported` | Gray | Data entered, not started |
| `permit_process` | Amber | Permit application in progress |
| `permit_ready` | Green | Permit released, ready for work |
| `implementasi` | Blue | Physical work on-site |
| `rfi_done` | Indigo | Ready for Inspection done |
| `rfs_done` | Violet | Ready for Service done |
| `bast` | Pink | BAST handover in progress |
| `invoice` | Rose | Invoice submitted |
| `completed` | Emerald | Fully done |

---

## 4. Site Detail Page (`/sites/{siteId}`)

The Site Detail page is a **read-only container** — no work is done here. It is a navigational hub.

```mermaid
graph TD
    SD["🏢 Site Detail Page\n/sites/{siteId}"]

    SD --> T1["Tab: Info Site\n(Site metadata, coordinates, technical specs)"]
    SD --> T2["Tab: Pekerjaan\n(List of all ATPs for this site)"]
    SD --> T3["Tab: Log\n(Combined activity log, grouped by ATP)"]

    T2 --> ROW["Each Row in ATP Table"]
    ROW --> FILL["Fill inline: ATP No, SOW, PO, Type, Stage, Status"]
    ROW --> BUKA["'Buka →' button"]
    BUKA --> ATP_PAGE["/atp/{id} — ATP Work Page"]

    style ATP_PAGE fill:#2563eb,color:#fff
```

### ATP Table — Inline Editable Columns

| Column | Input Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| ATP Number | Text | Click to edit · Click filled number to open work tab |
| SOW Project | Text | Click to edit |
| Asset Element | Text (monospace) | Click to edit |
| Capex Project | Text | Click to edit |
| PO Number | Text (monospace) | Click to edit |
| SOW ID | Text (monospace) | Click to edit |
| SOW Type | Text | Click to edit |
| Sector | Dropdown S1–S4 | Click to change |
| Type | Dropdown | FILTER / COMBAT / RESCOPING / BLACKSITE / L2H |
| Stage | Dropdown | Full stage list |
| Status | Dropdown | active / completed / cancelled / historical |
| Actions | Button | "Buka →" opens ATP Work Page as app tab |

---

## 5. One Active ATP Rule

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["Admin clicks '+ Tambah ATP'\nor changes Status → active"] --> B{Other active ATPs\non this site?}
    B -- Yes --> C["Previous active ATPs\nautomatically → 'historical'"]
    B -- No --> D["Proceed normally"]
    C --> D
    D --> E["New ATP is the\nsingle active work order"]

    style E fill:#059669,color:#fff
    style C fill:#d97706,color:#fff
```

> **Rule:** At any point in time, only **one** work order per site can have `status = active`.  
> All previous work orders are retained as `historical` for audit trail.

---

## 6. ATP Work Page — Tab Details

### 6.1 Permit Tab

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph Fields
        F1["Permit Status\n(dropdown)"]
        F2["Tower Provider"]
        F3["Create Date"]
        F4["Jenis Kunci\n(PADLOCK/SMARTLOCK/QUADLOCK)"]
        F5["Permit Start / Expiry"]
        F6["PIC Nama & Telp"]
        F7["TPAS / TP / CAF Nomor"]
    end

    subgraph Actions
        A1["📎 Upload Permit Docs"]
        A2["Simpan Draft"]
        A3["Update Stage Permit →\n(advances stage + saves all)"]
    end
```

> ⚠️ Permit Expiry turns **amber** if < 14 days left, **red** if expired.

### 6.2 Implementasi Tab

| Field | Input |
|---|---|
| Tim | Dropdown (teams filtered by project type) |
| Field Leader | Dropdown (leaders of selected team) |
| Tanggal Plan / Aktual | Date pickers |
| CI / CO Tanggal & Waktu | Date + time |
| RFI Done / RFS Done | Toggle checkboxes |
| Impl Status | Dropdown: Awaiting / Scheduled / On Going / RFS / Cancelled |
| Note Implementasi | Textarea |

### 6.3 ATP & Dokumen Tab

| Field | Input |
|---|---|
| PDID | Text |
| Tiket ATP | Text |
| Status ATP | Dropdown: REQUEST PDID / UPLOAD TAGGING DONE / TAGGING N/A / HOLD |
| Note Foto Evidence | Textarea |
| Azimuth S1 / S2 / S3 | Number inputs |

### 6.4 Penagihan Tab

Financial tracking table:
- All termin items (T1, T2a, T2b, T2c, T3, T4)
- Additional items: Biaya Perizinan, Transportasi, Material Tambahan
- Status per item: `draft → submitted → approved → paid`
- **[+ Tambah Item Pembayaran]** adds new row

### 6.5 Foto & File Tabs

| Tab | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Foto | Photo gallery — engineers upload from phone. Admin can add captions. |
| File & Lampiran | All non-photo documents, grouped: Permit Docs / Implementasi Docs / ATP Docs / Lainnya |

### 6.6 Log Tab

Chronological activity stream for **this ATP only**:
- Every field save, stage change, file upload is recorded
- Format: `[Avatar] Name · action · timestamp`

---

## 7. Auto-Save Behavior

All fields across **Permit**, **Implementasi**, and **ATP** tabs auto-save on blur (when user leaves the field). Selects and checkboxes save immediately on change.

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> idle
    idle --> saving : User leaves field (onBlur)\nor changes dropdown
    saving --> saved : ✓ Save successful
    saving --> error : ✗ Network/save failure
    saved --> idle : After 2 seconds
    error --> saving : User retries
```

### Save Status Indicator (top-right of each tab section)

| State | Display |
|---|---|
| `idle` | *(nothing shown)* |
| `saving` | `⏳ Menyimpan...` (gray) |
| `saved` | `✓ Tersimpan 14:32` (green, fades after 2s) |
| `error` | `✗ Gagal — Coba lagi` (red, stays until retry) |

> **[Update Stage] buttons** save **all pending fields first** before advancing the stage, ensuring no data loss even if the user hasn't explicitly saved.

---

## 8. Complete End-to-End Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant SiteList as Site List / Project Filter
    participant SiteDetail as Site Detail Page
    participant AtpTable as ATP Table (Pekerjaan Tab)
    participant AtpWorkPage as ATP Work Page
    participant MockDB as Mock Data Store

    alt Fast Path
        User->>SiteList: Click ATP Number in column
        SiteList->>AtpWorkPage: openTab() → /atp/{id}
    else Browse Path
        User->>SiteList: Click Site Name / Site ID
        SiteList->>SiteDetail: Navigate to /sites/{siteId}
        User->>SiteDetail: Click "Pekerjaan" tab
        SiteDetail->>AtpTable: Render ATP Work Order Table
        User->>AtpTable: Fill data inline (ATP No, PO, SOW...)
        AtpTable->>MockDB: Auto-save field on blur
        User->>AtpTable: Click "Buka →"
        AtpTable->>AtpWorkPage: openTab() → /atp/{id}
    end

    User->>AtpWorkPage: Edit Permit fields
    AtpWorkPage->>MockDB: Auto-save onBlur
    User->>AtpWorkPage: Click "Update Stage Permit →"
    AtpWorkPage->>MockDB: Save all + advance stage
    AtpWorkPage->>AtpWorkPage: Stepper updates visually

    User->>AtpWorkPage: Upload files / photos
    User->>AtpWorkPage: Submit Penagihan item
    User->>AtpWorkPage: View Log tab (this ATP only)
```

---

## 9. File & Component Map

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `src/pages/AtpWorkPage.tsx` | Main ATP work environment (`/atp/{id}`) |
| `src/pages/SiteDetail.tsx` | Site container page (`/sites/{siteId}`) |
| `src/pages/Sites.tsx` | Site registry with ATP links |
| `src/components/tables/ProjectSitesTable.tsx` | Project-filtered site table with ATP links |
| `src/components/work-orders/AtpTable.tsx` | Inline-editable ATP list inside SiteDetail |
| `src/components/modals/InitiationModal.tsx` | New ATP creation modal (enforces 1-active rule) |
| `src/hooks/useCellSave.ts` | Auto-save hook + 1-active enforcement |
| `src/context/TabContext.tsx` | App-tab state management |
| `src/data/mockData.ts` | `atpWorkOrders`, `workOrderLogs`, `siteMasterRecords` |

